# Addresses this repository may credit in a Co-authored-by trailer.
#
# The attribution gate (scripts/check-attribution.sh) rejects a Co-authored-by
# trailer unless the address it names appears in this file, matches the repo's
# configured git identity, or is passed via ATTRIBUTION_ALLOWLIST. Generator
# footers and Signed-off-by remain forbidden unconditionally.
#
# Why an allowlist at all: crediting the owner of this repository is not
# misattribution, but a gate cannot know that from the trailer's display name.
# "Hermes" is a real GitHub organization, so a name-keyed rule would look
# correct while crediting a stranger. The address is the identity anchor.
#
# This file is the auditable record, so it is TRACKED. An untracked copy is
# invisible to CI and to every other clone, which makes the same self-credit
# pass the local commit-msg hook and fail the MR job. tests/test-attribution-gate.sh
# asserts both presence and trackedness.
#
# In a merge request the gate reads this file from the TARGET branch, not from
# the branch under review, so an MR cannot widen the allowlist and spend the
# credit in the same MR. An entry added by an MR takes effect on the next merge.
#
# One address per line. Blank lines and #-comments are ignored. Changing this
# file is an attribution-policy change: review it like one.

# The GitHub noreply address the .gitmessage template offers. GitHub also accepts
# an ID-keyed spelling (6572003+iap@) which survives a username rename and is the
# more durable form; it is deliberately absent, so this repo credits the bare name.
iap@users.noreply.github.com